# Q22: append the joint core+envelope results to /output/report.json (idempotent: removes earlier Q22 entries first)
import json
R=json.load(open('/output/report.json'))
R['results']=[x for x in R['results'] if not x['quantity'].startswith('Q22')]
R['recipe']=[x for x in R['recipe'] if 'Q22' not in x['description']]
R['datasets']=[x for x in R['datasets'] if 'Q22' not in x.get('role','')]
A=[{"name":"model","value":"two uniform-sphere RADEX LVG zones (LAMDA HCN, HCO+; dv=150 km/s, N/dv not rescaled; grids out/q4c/grid4_*.npz, Tbg 2.73 K, 5 K as variant): core (T,n,N_HCN,N_HCO+, eta_core inside the Gaussian core, size from out/q4b/dilution.csv, Tint at 0.24 arcsec tied) + envelope (own T,n,N, filling we common to the 1.7, 5.7x3.5 and 10 arcsec apertures); flat priors log T 10-150 K, log n 3-8, log N 13-18.5, log eta/we -3..0; tempered SMC, 6000 particles, 2 seeds, evidence logZ + profile chi2 (BIC)"},
   {"name":"data","value":"1.7 arcsec deblended ladders (8 ratios, Q12b/Q20b, Harada+2018 1-0 ratios as labelled assumption) + Tint (0.24 arcsec core T_b, HCN & HCO+ 3-2) + 6 team-b p0028 10 arcsec intensities per nucleus (NOT independent of our deblend) with the Q20f error model (3% stat, aperture 10/3/5%, common per-band 10% flux scale shared by HCN and HCO+ in each aperture set, marginalised analytically); line width w for the 10 arcsec conversion free in 100-300 km/s; 1.7 arcsec nuisances g,h as Q12b. The 1.7 arcsec and 10 arcsec flux scales are treated as independent"},
   {"name":"geometry","value":"N and S 10 arcsec apertures overlap (separation ~5 arcsec) and are fitted separately; the envelope is assumed to cover both the 1.7 and the 10 arcsec apertures uniformly (lr variant: filling at 10 arcsec free in 0.1-1x)"}]
def res(q,t,v,u,un,c,e,extra=None):
    R['results'].append({"quantity":q,"target":t,"value":v,"uncertainty":u,"unit":un,"assumptions":A+(extra or []),"confidence":c,"evidence":e})
EV="scripts/q22_joint.py, q22_run.sh, q22_run2.sh, q22_post.py -> out/q22/runs/*.csv|npz, out/q22/q22_post.csv|log, run.log, run2.log"
res("Q22a: model comparison - the 10 arcsec ladders cannot be explained by the single-phase core of Q20 (dchi2 > 120); whether a SECOND TEMPERATURE is needed depends on the nucleus: N yes (dlnZ +23, dchi2 58 vs same-T), S no (same-T sparse extension preferred, dlnZ +2.9 over a hot envelope)",
 "S, N (1.7 + 10 arcsec, 16 data)",
 "Models (profile chi2 / free params k / ln evidence / BIC; Tbg 2.73 K, mean of 2 seeds), 16 data. S: M1 core-only (Gaussian-core dilution at 10 arcsec) 176.7/6/-115.3/193.3; M1E core + extended zone with the SAME (T,n,N) and own filling 9.3/7/-25.6/28.7; M2T shared T, different n,N 4.1/10/-30.0/31.9; M2 independent T 1.5/11/-28.5/32.0; M2H (Tc 10-25 K, Te 50-150 K = the hypothesis of the item) 1.5/11/-26.8/32.0. N: M1 135.1/6/-95.2/151.8; M1E 61.0/7/-54.9/80.4; M2T 2.8/10/-32.9/30.5; M2 2.8/11/-31.8/33.3; M2H 3.2/11/-31.0/33.7. On the 1.7 arcsec data alone (10 data, Q20 reproduced by M1): S M1 chi2 5.5/5 lnZ -18.9, M2 -19.3; N M1 11.2/5 lnZ -24.9, M2 -19.6 (the two-zone model removes the N Tint tension of Q20b). Reading: (i) core-only is excluded by the 10 arcsec ladder, as expected (core share at 10 arcsec 2-10%); (ii) S: M1E vs M2 dlnZ=+2.9 (BIC -3.3), vs M2H +1.2: the S 10 arcsec ladder does not require a hot envelope, it is fitted equally well by the same 20-30 K gas covering only ~1% of the 10 arcsec aperture; the hot envelope (M2H) is allowed (Bayes factor ~0.3 vs M1E, i.e. not excluded); (iii) N: single-state M1E is rejected (chi2 61 vs 2.8, pulls up to -4.7 sigma) and a two-zone solution is required, with the extended zone warmer: P(Tc>Te)=0.08 (M2). Robustness (N/S dlnZ M2-M1E; M2H-M1E): core size x1.5: S -0.7/+0.0, N +26/+27; free 10 arcsec envelope filling: S -1.6/-2.0 (M1E has 1 more parameter), N +22/+22; 10 arcsec flux-scale 15%: S -3.2/-1.8, N +25/+25; aperture errors x2: S -3.0/-2.2, N +17/+17; Tbg 5 K: S -2.3/-1.7, N +24/+24. The S preference for M1E is therefore only 0.7-3 in ln evidence (weak to moderate), the N two-zone requirement is robust.",
 "dlnZ spread between seeds 0.0-1.1; profile chi2 from Nelder-Mead on the 13/61-point nuisance grid","chi2, k, lnZ, BIC","medium",EV)
res("Q22b: P(T) and the cool-core/hot-envelope question for S: Tc = 18 [13,29] K (M2) / 24 [20,31] K (same-T), Te = 68 [38,106] K, P(Te>=50 K)=0.71 (prior 0.41) - the hot envelope is allowed, mildly favoured over nothing, not required",
 "S",
 "Posterior medians [16,84] (Tbg 2.73 K). M2 (independent T): Tc=18.2 [13.3,28.9] K, P(Tc<=25)=0.78, P(Tc<=30)=0.85; Te=68 [38,106] K, P(Te>=50)=0.71 (flat log-T prior gives 0.41; Tbg 5 K: Te 43 [29,65], Tc 17 [13,25]); P(Tc>Te)=0.10; eta_core=0.43 [0.26,0.62], we=0.12 [0.03,0.40], n_c=10^5.4 (4.98-6.4), n_e=10^4.3 (3.8-4.7), log N_HCN core 16.3 (15.6-16.9), envelope 15.5 (15.0-16.1); tau32(HCN) core 21 [4,71], envelope 1.1 [0.2,8.8]. M2H (hypothesis imposed): Tc=15.8 [11.7,20.4] K, Te=91 [67,121] K, eta_core 0.49 [0.34,0.70], we 0.24 [0.10,0.55]; lnZ -26.8 vs -28.5 (M2) and -25.6 (M1E). Same-T M1E: T=23.7 [19.7,30.8] K (Q20b: 19.6 [16.9,24.6] with 1.7 arcsec data only), eta_core 0.68 [0.56,0.83], extended filling 0.009, P(T>=50)=0.01. Shared-T two-density M2T: T=28 [22,40] K, core n 10^5.5, extended n 10^4.7, eta_core 0.22, we 0.04 (the 'clumpy' two-density variant). The core temperature is 15-30 K in every variant without an external floor; P(T) for the core never exceeds 40 K unless the CO floor (Q22d) is imposed.",
 "16-84%, SMC 2 seeds","K / probability","medium",EV)
res("Q22c: P(T) for N: a two-zone solution is required; extended-zone Te = 72 [46,105] K (P(Te>=50)=0.72), core Tc = 21 [12,42] K is poorly constrained (P(Tc<=25)=0.61)",
 "N",
 "M2 (Tbg 2.73 K): Tc=20.4 [11.4,42.3] K, Te=69 [43,112] K, P(Te>=50)=0.72, P(Tc>Te)=0.08, eta_core 0.50 [0.31,0.71], we 0.38 [0.14,0.75], n_c=10^5.8, n_e=10^4.3, log N_HCN core 16.3 (16.1-16.9), envelope 15.0 (14.6-15.6), tau32(HCN) core 19 [11,58], envelope 0.3 [0.1,1.0]. M2H: Tc 15.6 [11.4,21.2], Te 74 [57,106], lnZ -31.0 vs -31.8 (M2): the hypothesis is allowed and not distinguished. M2T (shared T): T=49 [37,73] K, P(T>=50)=0.48, lnZ -32.9. With Tbg 5 K the M2 labels are unstable (Tc 57, Te 41 K, P(Tc>Te)=0.57) while M2H gives Tc 19 [15,23], Te 72 [56,101]: N core vs envelope temperatures are not separated robustly; what is robust is that the data need a low-opacity extended component (tau32 ~0.3) and that a single (T,n,N) is rejected. This agrees qualitatively with p0028's warm 10 arcsec solution (Q20c: N 100 [80,134] K with a single zone, now 70 K with the two-zone core subtracted).",
 "16-84%","K / probability","medium",EV)
res("Q22d: external CO(2-1) temperature floor (p0040: S Tk>=30 K window-mean / >=40 K peak-channel, N >=18-21 K at ff=1) costs the S single-state model only dchi2=+0.9/+2.1 (dlnZ -1.1/-2.6): the 17-25 K S core of Q20 is mildly preferred, NOT required",
 "S, N",
 "Same fits with a Tk floor on both zones (Q20_TMIN). S, floor 30 K: M1E chi2 10.2 (free 9.3), lnZ -26.8 (free -25.6), T=34 [31,41] K, eta_core 0.76; M2 chi2 4.1 lnZ -30.2, Tc 40 [32,63], Te 53 [37,78]; M2T T=38 [32,53] K. Floor 40 K: M1E chi2 11.4, lnZ -28.2, T=44 [41,51] K, eta_core 0.82; M2 lnZ -29.7, Tc 53 [43,80] K. N floor 20 K: no change (M2 lnZ -31.4, Tc 37 [25,69]; M2T 62 [46,80] K); M1E still rejected. Consequence: with the CO floor the S dense-gas temperature is 34-44 K with eta_core 0.76-0.82 (a nearly space-filling core); without it 18-24 K with eta_core 0.4-0.7. The two are statistically indistinguishable with the present HCN/HCO+ ladders (dlnZ <=2.6, <2.3 sigma). The CO floor refers to the CO-bright gas and need not apply to the dense HCN-emitting gas; it is used here as an optional prior (CO ff prior of p0040: ff(0.26 arcsec)~0.7-0.8 for S).",
 "dchi2 and dlnZ from 2 seeds","K","medium",EV+"; scripts/q22_run2.sh; CO floor from /snapshots/team-a-s19 (p0040, out/q32/tk2.json)",
 [{"name":"CO floor","value":"p0040 ff=1 Tk lower limits applied to every zone; the CO and HCN gas are assumed co-located for this test only"}])
res("Q22e: abundance / path-length, H13CN(4-3) and mass consequences of the two-zone solution (X(HCN) 1e-9..3e-8)",
 "S, N",
 "Core path length L_c=N_H2/n with N_H2=N_HCN/X: S M2 X=1e-8 L_c=2.5 [0.05,23] pc, X=1e-9 25 [0.5,228] pc; S same-T M1E X=1e-8 11 [2.5,61] pc, X=1e-9 107 [25,606] pc; N M2 X=1e-8 1.4 [0.1,4.1] pc, X=1e-9 14 [1,41] pc. Requiring L_c<=66 pc (core size) and L_e<=500 pc keeps the fraction f of the posterior: S M1E 0.43/0.59/0.86/1.0, S M2 0.61/0.82/0.96/1.0, N M2 0.80/0.96/0.99/1.0 for X=1e-9/3e-9/1e-8/3e-8 (dlnZ=ln f: -0.2 to -0.8 for X=1e-9, i.e. X<=1e-9 is mildly disfavoured, not excluded; with the CO floor 40 K S M1E f=0.21 for 1e-9 and 0.60 for 1e-8, dlnZ -1.6/-0.5). For X=1e-8 the path (1-60 pc) is below the core size (50-90 pc): the core is clumpy (volume filling ~0.03-0.2 at n~1e5-3e5) rather than a uniform sphere, as the item anticipated. H13CN(4-3) test (limits HCN/H13CN >4 S, >8.3 N; applied to the summed core+envelope 1.7 arcsec 4-3 flux; R=12C/13C=30/50/100): fraction of posterior consistent S M2 0.54/0.71/0.90, S M1E 0.50/0.71/0.97, N M2 0.08/0.28/0.65 (N needs R>~50-100 or tau43 below ~5; N M2H 0.11/0.25/0.65). Masses (X=1e-8, mu=2.8 m_H, core size 0.455/0.507 arcsec pedestal-inclusive, envelope = the 10 arcsec aperture area pi*(5\")^2; scale as 1e-8/X, x0.3 for the Q5 Gaussian core size): S M2 M_core=1.5e8 [0.3,5.5e8], M_env(10\")=2.5e9 [1e9,5.9e9] Msun, core mass fraction of the HCN-traced gas in the 10 arcsec aperture 0.06 [0.01,0.22]; S M1E 0.18 [0.13,0.27]; N M2 0.09 [0.02,0.45] (M_core 2.6e8, M_env 2.0e9). With a Gaussian core (s=0.25 arcsec, x0.3) M_core(S)~5e7 ~ Mdyn(S,48 pc)=0.58e8 (Q5f). The core therefore holds ~5-20% of the dense gas within 10 arcsec, the envelope the rest; both fractions depend on the shared X and the assumed envelope extent.",
 "16-84% posterior; masses factor ~2-3 systematic (X, size, envelope extent)","pc, Msun, fraction","low",EV)
res("Q22f: verdict on the item: the joint two-component fit is not better than a single-state (same T) core + sparse extension for S (dlnZ -2.9 for the hot-envelope model), but is strongly required for N (dlnZ +23); P(T) for the S core is 15-24 K without and 34-44 K with the CO floor",
 "S, N",
 "Summary of Q22a-e. (1) A single-phase core cannot fit the 10 arcsec ladders (core carries 2-10% of the 10 arcsec flux). (2) S: single-state gas at 24 [20,31] K (core eta 0.68, extended filling 1%) is preferred over core 18 K + envelope 68 K by dlnZ 2.9, BIC 3.3, though the hot-envelope solution (Te>=50 K, P=0.71; M2H: Te 91 [67,121]) is not excluded; the p0028 'Tk>=50 K at 10 arcsec' and the Q20 'cool core 17-25 K' are compatible both with a single state of ~20-45 K covering ~1% of 10 arcsec (sparse clumps) and with a hot extended low-opacity envelope. (3) N: temperatures differ: core ~20 [12,42] K, envelope 72 [46,105] K, tau32(env)~0.3; the N-S contrast in the extended zone is not significant (Te 68 vs 69 K), in the core it is not significant (18 vs 20 K). (4) The previous statement 'two-phase S (Q16 geometry)' is not required by the data for S; for N it is. Not tested: independent 10 arcsec data (all are team-b p0028), uv-plane matching of the apertures, a shared envelope between N and S, and a Tbg>2.73 K from IR pumping.",
 "see Q22a-e","dimensionless","medium",EV)
R['recipe'].append({"order":max(x['order'] for x in R['recipe'])+1,"stage":"statistical_analysis","description":"Q22: q22_joint.py (derived from q20b_eta.py): models M1 (core only), M1E (same-state extended zone), M2T, M2, M2H on 1.7 arcsec ladders + Tint + team-b 10 arcsec ladders (Q20f error model); tempered SMC 6000 particles x 2 seeds, grids out/q4c Tbg 2.73 and 5 K; variants: core size x1.5 (Q20_TSC), free 10 arcsec envelope filling (Q22_LR), 10 arcsec scale 15% (Q22_SG), aperture error x2 (Q22_APS), Tk floors 30/40/20 K from the CO limits (q22_run2.sh); q22_post.py: P(T), abundance path-length cut (X 1e-9..3e-8), H13CN(4-3), masses; build_report_q22.py","scripts":["scripts/q22_joint.py","scripts/q22_run.sh","scripts/q22_run2.sh","scripts/q22_post.py","scripts/build_report_q22.py"],"software":"numpy, scipy, pandas, RADEX grids"})
R['datasets'].append({"files":["out/q4c/grid4_hcn.npz","out/q4c/grid4_hco+.npz","out/q1/q1_deblend_ladders_xb4f.csv","out/q4b/dilution.csv"],"content":"RADEX grids, 1.7 arcsec deblended ladders, 0.24 arcsec core T_b and sizes, team-b p0028 10 arcsec intensities (hard-coded as in q20f)","role":"Q22 joint core + envelope fit"})
